example: shuffle is a permutation of [1, 2, 3] true
reset gives [1, 2, 3] true
shuffle again is a permutation true
one element: 42
no elements: 0
repeated values: 1000 shuffles keep them true
3 elements, 60000 shuffles: all 6 orders equally likely true
4 elements, 48000 shuffles: all 24 orders equally likely true
5 elements, 60000 shuffles: all 120 orders equally likely true
50 elements, 20000 shuffles: element 0 lands evenly true
reset after 20000 shuffles gives 0..49 true
